This directory contains some Turing machine simulations.  It uses
../../scheme/prologue/turing-machine.rkt to run them.


RUNNING A SIMULATION

To run a machine, write a file, say utm_shiftright.tm, and
then use a command line like this.

ftpmaint@millstone:~/Documents/computing/src/lab/machines$ ../../scheme/prologue/turing-machine.rkt -f utm_shiftright.tm -c "S" -r "1BT1B1" -l "11B" -s 100 > utm_shiftright.out

Here, -c is the character under the head, -r is the tape to the right of the
head, -l is the tape to the left of the head, and -s is a limit on the number
of steps the machine performs.


TESTING

Note also the presence of a unit tester for those machines, 
machine_test.py.
